39 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186489629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490139 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "72ba71ce-b94a-5573-a9f5-03870c73d863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186489817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490167 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a4ad95fd-3ba5-57ea-89a2-4cf27fe1615b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186489704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490174 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b9111900-5b3b-528e-bee1-da24812f7bc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186489927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186489905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490205 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f8d3f67a-8384-5a77-a9a4-eb3e9f68a0eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162160" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490212 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following represents the streamlines of the vector field $F(x,y)=(\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}})i+(\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}})j$ over the domain $D=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>{x}^{2}\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03021383-b99c-5e38-823a-268b5d1215a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490212 #edb/ref 1074 "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=(\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}})i+(\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}})j\n$$\n\n is a vector field with simply connected domain $D,$ where $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}$ and $Q(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=\\frac{2x}{(y-{x}^{2})^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-\\frac{2x}{(y-{x}^{2})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=\\frac{2x}{(y-{x}^{2})^{2}}+(-\\frac{2x}{(y-{x}^{2})^{2}})=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}=-\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2})+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2})+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curves of the stream function $ψ(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2})$ given by the equations $ψ(x,y)=c.$\n\nNotice that the range of $ψ(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2}) & =c \\\\ y-{x}^{2} & ={e}^{c} \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}+{e}^{c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of parabolas with the vertex at $(0,{e}^{c}).$ Therefore, the correct graph (along with the vector field $F$) is as follows:\n\n![](images/ed/edc12146ffad4dc46ed6d57b3dfdc9a08ca92fb601ef5e08ed9ccef3a1c1da4c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490304 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490304 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162510" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490304 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490304 #edb/ref 1071 "Construct the vector field that has the stream function $ψ(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{1-y}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490304 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cae20d6b-2ae5-5a13-a8c2-7e9cf70b768d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490304 #edb/ref 1074 "A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if the following equations hold:\n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}\n$$\n\nComputing the partial derivatives of the function $ψ(x,y),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{1-y}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}{e}^{1-y}, \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{1-y}) \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{1-y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field with the stream function $ψ(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{1-y}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & =P\\,i+Q\\,j \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}{e}^{1-y}\\,i-2x{e}^{1-y}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490314 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490314 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490314 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490314 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,i-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j$\n\nII. $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=x\\,i+2{e}^{y}\\,j$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490314 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0611f00-dc8b-5374-b5f7-8b0d695e2534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490314 #edb/ref 1074 "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =2{e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=1+2{e}^{y}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186490205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490318 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162614" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490318 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490318 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-xy\\,j$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,i+({y}^{2}-2xy)\\,j$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,i-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y)\\,j$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9691dde-e78b-59c1-ac5c-550cb0f124bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490318 #edb/ref 1074 "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2x+(-x)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2x-2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =2y-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=(2x-2y)+(2y-2x)=0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III does have a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)+(-3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
